.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
File targets allow logs to be sent to a specified file\&. 

Files are created as needed, and logs are appended to any existing contents\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP Logging to file targets is thread safe\&. A mutex is used to coordinate writes to the file\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP Logging to file targets is not signal safe, as a non-reentrant lock is used to coordinate writes to the file\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP Logging to file targets is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the cleanup of the lock may not be completed\&. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void stumpless_close_file_target (struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * target)"

.PP
Closes a file target\&. This function closes the file target, as well as the stream opened to the file\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Unsafe\fP This function is not thread safe as it destroys resources that other threads would use if they tried to reference this target\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the destruction of a lock that may be in use as well as the use of the memory deallocation function to release memory\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the cleanup of the lock may not be completed, and the memory deallocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItarget\fP The file target to close\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
